In .NET 10 (MAUI), `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` was deprecated/removed because Android itself deprecated `SOFT_INPUT_ADJUST_RESIZE`. The recommended approach is now **edge-to-edge rendering with `WindowInsets` handling**.

## Solution

In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Android.OS.Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        // Enable edge-to-edge
        WindowCompat.SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(Window!, false);

        // Listen for keyboard (IME) insets and apply padding
        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(Window!.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content)!, 
            new InsetsListener());
    }

    private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var systemBarInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.SystemBars());

            // Use the larger of IME or system bar bottom inset
            int bottomPadding = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, systemBarInsets.Bottom);
            v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottomPadding);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

## Why this works

- **`SetDecorFitsSystemWindows(false)`** opts into edge-to-edge, giving your app the full window area.
- **`WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()`** reports the keyboard height. When the keyboard opens, `imeInsets.Bottom` becomes non-zero and you apply it as padding, pushing your content (and input bar) up.

## Tips

- Remove any old `Window.SetSoftInputMode(...)` or `[Activity(WindowSoftInputMode = ...)]` calls.
- If you use a `ScrollView` or `CollectionView` for messages, it will automatically adjust to the reduced space.
- For iOS, MAUI already handles keyboard avoidance via `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` — no extra work needed.
